<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">Does Veras work with other 3D software besides SketchUp and Revit?</div><div class="faq-answer">Currently, Veras AI is only available as plugins for SketchUp and Revit. Support for other platforms like Rhino and ArchiCAD is being considered based on user demand.</div></div>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">How does Veras AI compare to traditional render engines?</div><div class="faq-answer">Veras is much faster and easier to use than traditional engines like V-Ray or Corona, but offers less precise control. It's ideal for concept renders and client presentations, while traditional engines are better for final marketing materials requiring exact specifications.</div></div>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">Can I use Veras renders for commercial projects?</div><div class="faq-answer">Yes, all subscription plans include commercial usage rights. You can use Veras renders in client presentations, marketing materials, and portfolio work without additional licensing fees.</div></div>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">What happens if I exceed my monthly render limit?</div><div class="faq-answer">On Starter and Professional plans, you'll need to upgrade or wait until the next billing cycle. The Studio plan offers unlimited renders. You can also purchase additional render credits if needed.</div></div>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">How detailed does my model need to be?</div><div class="faq-answer">Veras works best with simple massing models that clearly define spaces and major elements. The AI fills in realistic details, so you don't need fully detailed models—basic geometry with clear intent is sufficient.</div></div>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">Can I control the level of photorealism?</div><div class="faq-answer">Yes, Veras offers multiple rendering styles from sketch-like to highly photorealistic. You can use text prompts to guide the AI toward your desired aesthetic, and adjust materials and lighting as needed.</div></div>
